  "problem": "How many diagonals does a pentagon $ABCDE$ have?",
  "worked_solution": "Diagonals join non-adjacent vertices.\n\nAs we can see from the diagram below, the diagonals of the pentagon are $\\overset{―}{AC},$ $\\overset{―}{AD},$ $\\overset{―}{BD},$ $\\overset{―}{BE}$ and $\\overset{―}{CE}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133876/assets/b3956aebca9c5cf83a42b72de049d3a2c2e91604e336ae3d1d62ba2d8e22d315.png)\n\nTherefore, the pentagon $ABCDE$ has $5$ diagonals.",
